This license covers everything in the Medalluin project: the source code,
the artwork, textures and other images, the generators and tools that produce
them, and the documentation. That includes the project as published on GitHub
and on CurseForge, in every version (together, "the Work"). The only
exceptions are the third-party material listed in section 7.

The Work is not open source. Being able to read it does not give you the
right to reuse it. The only rights you have are the ones granted below; all
others are reserved by the author.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. Download the Work from its official sources (section 8), install it,
      and use it to play World of Warcraft.

   b. Read and study the source code.

   c. Change your own installed copy for your own personal use, for example
      to adjust a colour, a size or a position. A changed copy must stay on
      your own computer.

   d. Take screenshots and record videos of the Work in use, and publish
      them (streams, guides and reviews included), as long as the Work is
      named as "Medalluin" where that is reasonable to do.

   e. Link to the Work's official pages.

   f. Submit issues and pull requests to the official GitHub repository,
      under section 4.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Unless the author has given you written permission, you may not:

   a. redistribute, reupload, mirror or share the Work, or any part of it,
      in any form, changed or unchanged. This includes other addon sites,
      file hosts, UI packs, compilations and installers. Point people to the
      official sources instead.

   b. publish or distribute anything based on the Work. This includes forks,
      ports, retextures, reskins, "edits", and addons that copy its code,
      its art or its layout.

   c. present the Work, or anything based on it, under a different name or
      as anyone else's work, or remove or change the author's name,
      copyright notices or this license.

   d. use the name "Medalluin", its logo or its artwork to name, advertise
      or identify any other project, or in a way that suggests the author
      endorses it.

   e. sell the Work, charge for access to it, or bundle it with anything
      that is sold. This includes putting it behind a paywall, a
      subscription or a donation reward.

   f. use the Work, or any part of it, to train or fine-tune a
      machine-learning model, or to build a dataset for one.


3. PERMISSION

   To ask for anything section 2 does not allow, write to the author at
   contact@ahrymx.dev. Permission counts only when it is given in writing,
   and only to the extent the writing says.


4. CONTRIBUTIONS

   By submitting a contribution (code, art, text or anything else) to the
   official repository, you confirm that it is your own work or that you
   have the right to submit it. You also grant the author a perpetual,
   worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free license to use, change, distribute
   and relicense your contribution as part of the Work or separately from
   it, under any terms the author chooses. You keep your own copyright in
   your contribution. Submitting a contribution does not give you any right
   to the rest of the Work beyond what this license grants.


5. ENDING OF RIGHTS

   If you break this license, every right it gives you ends at once,
   without notice. Ending your rights does not limit anything else the
   author can do about the breach.


